{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationSymmetricDeltaExcluded","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationSymmetricDeltaExcluded","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEven_nonzero_implies_asymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEven_nonzero_implies_asymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationSymmetricDeltaExcluded.lean#L68-L75","doc":"Contrapositive form: if the bar-even total is nonzero (as for the deuteron `g₂ ≠ 0`), the dressing\nis **not** conjugation-symmetric — it must differ on some conjugate pair `Δ_λ ≠ Δ_{λ'}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEvenTotal_symmetric_zero_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEvenTotal_symmetric_zero_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationSymmetricDeltaExcluded.lean#L57-L66","doc":"**The exclusion (deuteron, `sgn = −1`): a conjugation-symmetric dressing kills the bar-even\ntotal.** If `Δ (c p) = Δ p` for all `p`, then `barEvenTotal (−1) c T Δ = 0`. Hence no\nconjugation-symmetric `Δ_λ` can supply the deuteron's nonzero bar-even coefficient `g₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEvenTotal_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEvenTotal_eq","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationSymmetricDeltaExcluded.lean#L49-L55","doc":"**Per-block form** of the bar-even total: `∑ T_λ · (Δ_λ + sgn·Δ_{λ'})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEvenTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barEvenTotal","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationSymmetricDeltaExcluded.lean#L44-L47","doc":"The (unnormalised) **bar-even total** of the `Δ`-dressed Wedderburn sum `S = ∑ T_λ Δ_λ`:\n`S + sgn · (bar image of S)`, with `sgn = (−1)^{n-1}` the weight bar-sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.sum_reindex_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.sum_reindex_conj","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationSymmetricDeltaExcluded.lean#L35-L42","doc":"**Reindexing over the conjugation involution.** For a permutation `c` with `c (c p) = p`,\n`∑ T (c p) · Δ p = ∑ T p · Δ (c p)` — the bar image can be moved from `T` onto `Δ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}